# .dockerignore — keeps secrets and cruft out of the Docker build context.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS: Dockerfile.netadmin does `COPY . /app`. On the Mac mini the
# context is a git-archive tar (tracked files only), so secrets never enter. But
# the buildx path (deploy/build-multiarch.sh, amd64 users) can build straight from
# a working tree, where an unignored `COPY .` would bake data/secrets.env, the live
# SQLite DB, and node_modules into an image layer. This file makes every `docker
# build` / `docker buildx build` from the repo root secret-safe by construction.
#
# Mirrors the secret/output rules in .gitignore; keep the two in sync.

# --- Secrets: never, under any circumstances ---
**/secrets.env
**/*.env
!**/*.env.example
data/deploy_hosts.env
.jwt_secret

# --- Local state / generated data ---
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/netadmin.db*
reports/
Logging/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- VCS + tooling ---
.git
.gitignore
.github/
.clubhouse/
.claude/
.mcp.json

# --- Frontend build inputs (web/dist is the only artifact the image wants;
#     node_modules and sources are not) ---
web/node_modules/
web/src/
web/public/
web/*.config.*
web/package*.json
web/tsconfig*.json
web/index.html
web/.vite/

# --- Test suite and dev-only trees (the daemon runtime imports none of these) ---
tests/
Archive/

# --- Docker / deploy scaffolding that need not live inside the image ---
# (Docker reads the Dockerfile named by -f regardless of these rules; they only
# keep the scaffolding out of the COPY . layer.)
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
docker-bake.hcl
docker-compose.yml
deploy/artifacts/

# --- Home Assistant add-on: describes how to build an image, so it has no
#     business being inside one. The add-on installs the published wheel. ---
addon/
repository.yaml
